Archived part3 typed-date sort/filter workflows
=============================================

Fresh first-party behavior adaptation of the two preserved part3 official
source/proxy workflows, supplied by the author under Apache-2.0.
Complete terms remain in LICENSE-APACHE-2.0. Original identities and SHA256:
part3/pyqt-official-ports/ports/itemviews/pyqt-official/basicsortfiltermodel-9dab02b61cebbdb7.py:
cecf5221bfc7da755664069fb316696c5144e4437d97d325b32431bbf89c1621
part3/pyqt-official-ports/ports/itemviews/pyqt-official/customsortfiltermodel-029ea0dabe87ae57.py:
a844adb5f7888373586f0e37f81025d991c19b96d5e205fdd376258a712c6e2d
Changes: complete current-font glyph metadata in place of synthetic mail;
typed Qt dates, default-locale date matching, original native-regexp/date-range/
case-sensitive comparator policies; explicit dates/default repairs, read-only
views and owned lifetime. Native timestamps use a local copy with exact epoch
fences; an optional scalar epoch channel prevents typed-cell precision loss.
No original body/resource is executed or bundled. The existing part2 semantics
remain separate.

